      <div class="article__main">
        <div class="article__body prose">
          <blockquote>
<ul>
<li><strong>Quick answer:</strong> The map is a US state called <strong>Leonida</strong>. Rockstar North’s Aaron Garbut says it is about <strong>twice the size of GTA 5’s map</strong>. The exact size is <strong>not announced</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>It has 6 regions.</strong> The names are hidden below in a spoiler block, if you want to stay surprised.</li>
<li><strong>Free printable map:</strong> Rockstar says a printable poster and Leonida map go on its GTA VI website on launch day (19 Nov). Check it is live before you link to it.</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Words used on this page.</strong> <em>Region</em> is a big area of the map. <em>Spoiler block</em> is a box you open to read. Open it only if you want that information.</p>
<h2 id="how-big-is-it" tabindex="-1">How big is it?</h2>
<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="table">
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Claim</th>
<th>Who said it</th>
<th>Label</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>About <strong>2x GTA 5’s map</strong></td>
<td>Aaron Garbut (Rockstar North) to Game Informer, reported by Forbes and Mapheist</td>
<td>Developer statement, reported</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>About <strong>3x Red Dead Redemption 2</strong> (playable area)</td>
<td>Rob Nelson (Rockstar), via GameSpot; the 3x detail was relayed by a secondary site citing the New York Times</td>
<td>Reported, secondary</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Exact area in km² or miles</td>
<td>Nobody. Rockstar has published no figure.</td>
<td>Not announced</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Rumour / unconfirmed:</strong> A community-made map (YANIS v16) measures Leonida’s land at about <strong>85.6 km²</strong>, a figure relayed by Notebookcheck and summarised by Mapheist. This is a fan estimate, not a Rockstar number. Source: <a href="https://mapheist.com/en/news/gta-6-game-informer-cover-story/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">https://mapheist.com/en/news/gta-6-game-informer-cover-story/</a></p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Rumour / unconfirmed:</strong> Forbes’ “58.6 square miles” is the writer’s own sum (twice GTA 5’s area). It is not from Rockstar. Source: <a href="https://www.forbes.com/sites/brianmazique/2026/10/06/gta-6s-map-is-about-twice-the-size-of-gta-5-with-hurricanes-and-170-animal-species/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">https://www.forbes.com/sites/brianmazique/2026/10/06/gta-6s-map-is-about-twice-the-size-of-gta-5-with-hurricanes-and-170-animal-species/</a></p>
</blockquote>
<h2 id="the-free-printable-map" tabindex="-1">The free printable map</h2>
<ol>
<li>Go to <strong><a href="http://rockstargames.com/VI" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">rockstargames.com/VI</a></strong> on launch day, 19 November 2026.</li>
<li>Look for the printable poster and Leonida map.</li>
<li>Download it and print it.</li>
</ol>
<p>Rockstar says a double-sided paper poster is also on the Rockstar Store for <strong>$0.99</strong>, or free with any Rockstar Store purchase after launch (USA Today, VGC). <em>The link goes live on 19 Nov. Verify before publishing the link.</em></p>
<p>![<a href="http://rockstargames.com/VI" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">rockstargames.com/VI</a> page area where the map download sits](TODO: image:map-step-1 — step screenshot (own screenshot, credit Rockstar): the VI page with the printable map link highlighted, after it goes live)
<em>Caption: Step screenshot. Where the free printable map is on the official site.</em></p>
<h2 id="weather-and-wildlife" tabindex="-1">Weather and wildlife</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Weather</strong> is local and keeps going. It can rain in one place while it is sunny next to it. <strong>Hurricanes</strong> are in the game. How often they happen is not announced. (Game Informer cover story, via Forbes)</li>
<li><strong>Wildlife:</strong> <strong>170+</strong> animal species, including <strong>60+</strong> bird types and <strong>30+</strong> land mammals. They are sorted as <strong>Rare, Discoverable and Legendary</strong>. (Forbes)</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="regions-of-leonida" tabindex="-1">Regions of Leonida</h2>
<p>Leonida has <strong>6</strong> regions. Their names are shown in Rockstar’s official material. Open the box to see them.</p>
<details class="spoiler"><summary class="spoiler__summary"><span class="spoiler__label">The 6 region names (no story, names only)</span><span class="spoiler__hint" aria-hidden="true">tap to reveal</span></summary><div class="spoiler__body" data-pagefind-ignore>
<ul>
<li>Vice City</li>
<li>Leonida Keys</li>
<li>Grassrivers</li>
<li>Port Gellhorn</li>
<li>Ambrosia</li>
<li>Mount Kalaga National Park</li>
</ul>
<p>Sources: Rockstar’s GTA VI character page links to some of these regions. Forbes and PC Gamer list all six. For what each region is like, see the <a href="leonida.md">Leonida hub</a>.</p>
</div></details>
<p>![simple diagram of Leonida regions with empty labels](TODO: image:map-step-2 — diagram, our own art (not the leaked or fan maps): a plain outline of Leonida with six numbered regions, names added once confirmed)
<em>Caption: Diagram. Our own sketch of the six regions. It is not to scale.</em></p>
<h2 id="place-names" tabindex="-1">Place names</h2>
<details class="spoiler"><summary class="spoiler__summary"><span class="spoiler__label">Named places from official store text (no story)</span><span class="spoiler__hint" aria-hidden="true">tap to reveal</span></summary><div class="spoiler__body" data-pagefind-ignore>
<p>Rockstar’s Ultimate Edition store text names <strong>Gambit Bay, Washington Beach, Watson Bay, Mount Kalaga, Southside Vice City, Stockyard</strong> and <strong>Lake Leonida</strong>. Polygon also lists <strong>Ocean Beach</strong> and <strong>Shore Drive</strong> from the Vintage Vice City Pack text. The store texts do not always say which region each place is in.</p>
</div></details>
<h2 id="in-game-map" tabindex="-1">In-game map</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Map style, markers, fast travel:</strong> not announced by Rockstar.</li>
<li>One preview reports that the menu map looks like <strong>satellite photos</strong> (Mapheist, citing Game Informer). Treat this as reported.</li>
<li>We will add our own <strong>interactive map</strong> after launch, when players have checked the pins.</li>
</ul>
<p>![map pin legend for our future interactive map](TODO: image:map-step-3 — map pin diagram, our own art: pin shapes for shops, garages, collectibles, activities)
<em>Caption: Map pin. The icons our interactive map will use.</em></p>
<h2 id="faq" tabindex="-1">FAQ</h2>
<h3 id="how-big-is-the-gta-6-map" tabindex="-1">How big is the GTA 6 map?</h3>
<p>About twice GTA 5’s map, per Rockstar North’s Aaron Garbut. The exact size is not announced.</p>
<h3 id="how-many-regions-are-in-gta-6" tabindex="-1">How many regions are in GTA 6?</h3>
<p>Six. The names are in the spoiler box above.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-get-a-paper-map" tabindex="-1">Can I get a paper map?</h3>
<p>Rockstar offers a free printable one on its website from launch day. A double-sided poster is $0.99 at the Rockstar Store.</p>
<h3 id="are-there-hurricanes" tabindex="-1">Are there hurricanes?</h3>
<p>Yes. Hurricanes are part of the weather system. How often is not announced.</p>
